      "description": "Open air museum Mühlenhof, Münster, North Rhine-Westphalia, GermanyThe Mühlenhof Open-Air Museum was founded in 1961 with the aim of preserving historic buildings and craftsmanship from the region. In 1963, the museum officially opened its doors to visitors, who have since had the opportunity to experience rural life of past centuries up close. Over time, the museum has been continuously expanded, with additional buildings illustrating different aspects of rural life and craftsmanship. In the 1980s, a mill complex was added to the museum, highlighting the Mühlenhof (mill farm) that gave it its name.",
